# Context

## Background
README, ARCHITECTURE and BACKLOG still described OpenCode with the
old per-message JSON storage model and listed Codex/Pi format
verification as open work.

## Why This Way
The verification on this machine (NOTES.md, 2026-11-13) resolved
both: formats are confirmed, and OpenCode v2 stores sessions in
SQLite, which changes the phase 2 spike from "verify enumerated
file storage" to "design a poll-based cursor".

## Gotchas
